 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "In a bar in Spain",
     "texto": [
      "In Spain it is very common to meet up with **¿Tomamos algo?** People stand at **la barra** or sit at a table and share **tapas** (small portions) or **raciones** (larger ones). Words and customs change by region.\n\nWith the waiter people often use **tú**: **¿Nos pones** una caña**?** **¿Me pones** un refresco con hielo**?** To repeat: **otra de lo mismo**.\n\nTo ask what a dish contains you use **llevar**: **¿lleva** carne? To say food tastes good you use **estar** and the adjective agrees: el plato está **rico**; las croquetas están **ricas**.\n\nFriends take turns paying: **hoy invito yo**; **te invito yo**. For the bill: **la cuenta, por favor**. If you do not eat meat: **soy vegetariano** or **vegetariana**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«Llevar», «estar rico» and asking with «pones»",
     "texto": [
      "Three useful uses in a bar:\n\n- **llevar** = to have as an ingredient: **¿lleva carne?**, **las croquetas llevan jamón**.\n- **estar + rico**: the adjective agrees with the dish: **rico, rica, ricos, ricas**.\n- **¿Me pones…?** and **¿Nos pones…?** with **tú** to the waiter. With **usted** it would be **¿Me pone…?**"
     ],
